Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) via OIDC
To enhance access security, the IAM layer integrates Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) into the OpenID Connect (OIDC) flow through Keycloak. This approach adds an extra verification step beyond the standard username and password, ensuring that only verified users can access the Paladin and Validium environments. During the OIDC login process, Keycloak performs primary authentication using credentials or a federated IdP, followed by a secondary verification factor before issuing tokens. Supported MFA methods include TOTP codes generated by authenticator apps (such as Google or Microsoft Authenticator), as well as email or SMS-based verification, providing a robust and seamless security layer aligned with enterprise authentication standards